WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.481
JAMIE: I want to ask the question that's
probably on a few minds.

00:00:02.481 --> 00:00:04.963
JAMIE: These are balloons collecting
data. What kind of data are we talking

00:00:04.963 --> 00:00:07.444
JAMIE: about?

00:00:07.529 --> 00:00:11.454
ALEX: The reporting specifies
atmospheric data. WindBorne's product is
weather balloon technology. This

00:00:11.454 --> 00:00:15.380
ALEX: isn't a surveillance contract,
based on what TechCrunch reported.

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:19.671
JAMIE: I appreciate the precision.
Because "balloon data collection" in a
defense contract

00:00:19.671 --> 00:00:23.851
JAMIE: lands differently in 2026 than it
would have three years ago.

00:00:24.031 --> 00:00:27.874
RUFUS: Context being the Chinese balloon
incident that became a significant
diplomatic event

00:00:27.874 --> 00:00:31.717
RUFUS: in 2023. High-altitude balloon
programs and their data collection
capabilities are no

00:00:31.717 --> 00:00:35.560
RUFUS: longer a niche topic.
